From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:29:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dtoverlay: Refuse an override's offset outside a property

dtoverlay_extract_override() read a cell target's offset with atoi(),
which takes a sign: "prop:-4" makes dtoverlay_override_one_target()
write before the property's buffer, a zero-length allocation when the
property is absent, and an offset near INT_MAX overflows the length it
computes. Refuse both as a malformed override, as the other malformed
overrides are refused.
---
 dtmerge/dtoverlay.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dtmerge/dtoverlay.c b/dtmerge/dtoverlay.c
index 14a2ce1..487c7a5 100644
--- a/dtmerge/dtoverlay.c
+++ b/dtmerge/dtoverlay.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT
 SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 */
 
+#include <limits.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
@@ -2242,7 +2243,16 @@ static int dtoverlay_extract_override(const char *override_name,
         else
         {
             /* The target is a cell/integer */
-            *offp = atoi(prop_name + name_len + 1);
+            long off = strtol(prop_name + name_len + 1, NULL, 10);
+            /* A negative offset would patch before the property, and one
+               near INT_MAX overflows the length the patch needs */
+            if (off < 0 || off > INT_MAX - 8)
+            {
+                dtoverlay_error("  override %s: bad offset in '%.*s'",
+                                override_name, target_len, prop_name);
+                return -FDT_ERR_BADVALUE;
+            }
+            *offp = (int)off;
             *sizep = 1 << (strchr(offset_seps, sep) - offset_seps);
             type = DTOVERRIDE_INTEGER;
             dtoverlay_debug("  override %s: cell target %.*s @ offset %d (size %d)",
